          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "perficiō is built on faciō, \"to make, to do\", with per-, \"through\" (EtymDB): to do right through. English perfect comes from its participle."
            }
          ]
        },
